{"id": "EUVD-2026-102350", "enisaUuid": "e076581e-373d-35b9-80fa-385908ff8995", "description": "AdPlug through 2.4 contains a heap-based buffer overflow in CksmPlayer::update() in src/ksm.cpp that writes past the fixed databuf[2048] array without bounds checking. Attackers can supply a crafted .ksm module whose notes share one time slot to overflow the heap player object, causing memory corruption and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:17", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/adplug-ksm-note-loop-databuf-oob-write", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug/blob/e491e382479ed2246f124c96c70d94561dce59b9/src/ksm.cpp#L99-L229", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug/issues/292", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug/pull/295", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/adplug-through-2.4-heap-buffer-overflow-via-cksmplayer-update-in-ksm-cpp"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110875", "GHSA-jrh8-g7qr-96vg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f2032101-8b0e-3019-a06d-d781a79dca00", "product": {"name": "adplug", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8458be60-abeb-31dc-ba90-033f53a320e7", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}], "isExploited": false}